  "unresolved": [
    "Four official China photographs including a bare rear view were visually inspected. Focus, zoom and aperture rings and a focus-distance scale are visible, but complete Nikon Z-specific four-direction coverage is unavailable. The functions of individual unlabeled shift/rotation controls, rotation travel and aperture click behavior require a matching manual.",
    "China specifies 80 mm diameter x 98.91 mm length; Japan prints the dimensions in the opposite order and notes mount-dependent variation. Existing measurements are retained with this discrepancy and Z-specific scope unresolved. Approximately 575 g excludes caps in China and hood/caps in Japan; precise Z weight remains unconfirmed.",
    "The China table also gives full-frame angles 121.9-84 degrees, while Japan identifies APS-C coverage. Those angles are not used to expand the coverage claim without clarification of shift and vignetting limits. Existing APS-C angles lack stated orientation.",
    "Coating function, electronic contacts, environmental protection, external length behavior, supplied accessories and the focal length/conditions for 0.4x magnification remain unconfirmed. The official-site user experience article describes internal zoom but is not treated as a manufacturer specification. A matching manual was not found in the accessible index/search; the global product page was inaccessible."
